{"name":"Poodle Skirt Peach","hex":"#ea927a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"poodle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A breed of dog originating in Europe as hunting dogs, and having heavy, curly coat in a solid color; their shoulder height indicates their classification as standard, medium, miniature, or toy.","A person servile towards someone whom they consider their superior."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To wear a partial fursuit, typically the head and hands, while showing one's skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poodle"},{"term":"skirt","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A separate article of clothing, usually worn by women and girls, that hangs from the waist and covers the lower torso and part of the legs.","A similar part of a dress or robe, etc., that hangs below the waist."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be on or form the border of.","To move around or along the border of; to avoid the center of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skirt"},{"term":"peach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any tree of species Prunus persica, native to China and now widely cultivated throughout temperate regions, having pink flowers and edible fruit.","Soft juicy stone fruit of the peach tree, having yellow flesh, downy, red-tinted yellow skin, and a deeply sculptured pit or stone containing a single seed."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the color peach.","Particularly pleasing or agreeable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Poodle skirt","blocks":[{"text":"A poodle skirt is a wide swing felt skirt of a solid color displaying a design appliquéd or transferred to the fabric. The design was often a coiffed poodle. Later substitutes for the poodle patch included flamingoes, flowers, and hot rod cars. They quickly became very popular with teenage girls in 1950s, who wore them at school dances, and as everyday wear."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d0/The_Childrens_Museum_of_Indianapolis_-_Poodle_skirt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poodle_skirt"},{"title":"Poodle","blocks":[{"text":"The Poodle, called the Pudel in German and the Caniche in French, is a breed of water dog. The breed is divided into four varieties based on size, the Standard Poodle, Medium Poodle, Miniature Poodle and Toy Poodle, although the Medium Poodle is not universally recognised. They have a distinctive thick, curly coat that comes in many colours and patterns, with only solid colours recognised by major breed registries. Poodles are active and intelligent, and are particularly able to learn from humans. Poodles tend to live 10–18 years, with smaller varieties tending to live longer than larger ones."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Full_attention_%288067543690%29.jpg/330px-Full_attention_%288067543690%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poodle"},{"title":"Skirt","blocks":[{"text":"A skirt is the lower part of a dress or a separate outer garment that covers a person from the waist downwards."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Skirt.jpg/330px-Skirt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skirt"},{"title":"Peach","blocks":[{"text":"The peach is a deciduous tree that bears edible juicy fruits with various characteristics. Most are simply called peaches, while the glossy-skinned, non-fuzzy varieties are called nectarines. Though from the same species, they are regarded commercially as different fruits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg/330px-Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jp